    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/79756": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Police Officer (4275) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Police Officer (4275) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE Under general supervision, monitors and patrols District facilities, property, and surrounding areas for the purposes of performing law enforcement, emergency response, and crime prevention functions to provide a safe environment for students, staff, and the public. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Develops and implements a student-centered approach to community policing, focusing on student development and assistance. Patrols to detect and deter crime and to help when need Maintain effective liaison with local outside law enforcement agencies. (i.e., Marietta Police Department, Cobb County Sheriff's Office, GEMA, etc.) Ability to lead law enforcement efforts in response to critical incidents. Ability to manage third-party private security contracts. Prepares required reports. Checks the security of buildings. Investigates suspicious activities or persons. Investigates traffic accidents and criminal or non-criminal incidents. Makes arrests and issue citations to individuals who have committed a crime. Responds to emergency incidents. Provides security and traffic enforcement at special events. Respond to calls for maintenance issues and relay information as needed. Assist local jurisdictions as outline in the Georgia mutual aid act. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training and/or Experience Build and maintain positive working relationships with the public using principles of good customer service Sufficient experience to understand the basic principles relevant to the major duties of the position. Good standing with GA P.O.S.T Ability to successfully pass department background investigation. Ability to successfully pass Human Resources background investigation. Valid Georgia driver’s license. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Strong interpersonal skills, including the ability to promote vision, work ethic, and accountability in a team environment. Ability to model integrity, character and leadership for providing excellence in chiropractic to humanity. Ability to model optimal citizenship attributes in the Life community. Ability to maintain mental concentration for extended periods of time. Ability to perform multiple duties in addition to departmental responsibilities with competing pressures and distractions. Ability to manage time effectively. Ability to tolerate, implement and embrace change. Capability to analyze and effectively resolve relational conflicts in clinical and other situations under routine and crisis demands. Certifications, Licenses, registrations Must be Georgia P.O.S.T. certified Valid Georgia Driver’s License or eligible to obtain within 30 days of hire. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS AA or AS Degree in Criminal Justice from an accredited College/University and two (2) years of law enforcement experience. PHYSICAL DEMANDS Nature of work requires an ability to operate security vehicle, computer equipment, and radio. Requires ability to communicate and exchange information, collects, compiles, compares, and prepares work documents, set-up and maintain work files. Must be able to lift between 40 lbs individually and up to 100 lbs with assistance; retrieving and placing materials on high shelves and on floor-level shelves; standing, walking; carrying; grasping; hearing; seeing; sitting; kneeling; climbing; balancing; stooping; crouching and reaching. WORKING CONDITIONS Work is mostly performed in a general office environment. However, there are times that this individual will cover for other officers in the field or on another shift. Each officer must be certified in the use of police equipment such as a firearm, handcuffs, radio and baton. This department is available 24/7. This job description is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties or skills required for the job and is subject to review and change at any time, with or without notice, in accordance with the needs of Life University.  Since no job description can detail all the duties and responsibilities that may be required from time to time in the performance of a job, duties and responsibilities that may be inherent in a job, reasonably required for its performance, or required due to the changing nature of the job shall also be considered part of the jobholder’s responsibility. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/79749": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Campus Safety Officer (4276) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Campus Safety Officer (4276) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description PURPOSE Provides professional security services for the University campus by controlling access to all buildings; patrolling the grounds and facilities; providing written reports based on daily activities; and performing specific duties pertaining to the safety, security, peace and order, and public relations of the University campus community. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Follows daily requirements for building locking and unlocking procedures. Periodically inspects buildings and grounds during the shift to ensure there is no physical damage. Patrols parking lots regularly to ensure traffic flow is not disturbed. Writes parking tickets when necessary. Impounds unauthorized vehicles according to established procedures. Assists visitors, students, faculty, and employees with vehicle problems, directions, and information as requested. Participates in organized programs for training, crime prevention, and community relations. Writes reports as necessary according to department protocol and documents all incidents as required. Develops good working relationships with other campus departments, faculty, and students. Answers the telephone and relays information to the appropriate personnel. Performs all other duties as assigned to support the Life University mission. Locks and unlocks doors on campus and surrounding property. Maintains familiarity with and supports the mission of Life University and Campus Safety. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assumes additional responsibilities and performs special projects as needed or directed. Exhibits student-centeredness in the performance of all job duties. Treats all others with respect; understands the impact of culture and background on the behavior of others; respects differences among the Life community; and demonstrates inclusive behavior. Anticipates, listens to, understands, and responds to customer needs. Delivers work products and services to customers in a manner that reflects positively upon the department and the University. Handles incidents to help ensure the safety of police officers and other first responders. Monitors radio channels and provides immediate information and assistance to police and other first responders. Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training and/or Experience A High School Diploma (or equivalent) with some security or law enforcement experience. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics Possesses some knowledge of federal, state, and local laws and regulations. Able to perform duties independently under general supervision. Able to prioritize and manage multiple projects while adhering to strict timelines. Strong interpersonal skills with a focus on conflict resolution. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively at all levels. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving abilities. Able to organize work, engage in a variety of tasks simultaneously, and consistently meet deadlines. Able to write reports and business correspondence. Computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Ability to perform CPR and basic lifesaving activities. Ability to observe and define problems, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Certifications, Licenses, Registrations A valid Georgia Driver’s License is required. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/4273": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chiropractic Science (618) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Chiropractic Science (618) Hot Job Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Purpose The purpose of faculty is to fulfill the educational mission of the department, the college, and the university in cooperation with the other members of the department and others in the university community.  Faculty are responsible for didactic instruction of students in classrooms, laboratories, seminars, and other settings, as well as for professional practice instruction in clinics and other practice sites. Essential Job Functions Compliance with the Life University Honor Code as well as all University and college policies, including those in the Employee Handbook and the Faculty Handbook. Responsible for the instruction, supervision, evaluation and mentoring of students in and outside of the classroom and/or laboratory setting. On-going assessment of success in achieving learning goals of courses. Demonstrate assessment of success in achieving learning outcomes of course and program curricula. Maintenance of required academic records. Prepare a syllabus for each course taught according to the approved college template and post it to the respective Blackboard course. Remain current in the field of expertise Teach class in a professional manner, teaching the material that is present in the syllabus and course outline. Required to maintain and be available for student office hours for the primary purpose of communicating with students regarding assigned courses, mentoring and providing supplemental instruction, as required by the individual College. Attend faculty and departmental meetings, faculty development programs, or other meetings/events as required. Complete training as required by the individual College. Cultivate in oneself and others an attitude of helpfulness, personal commitment to building relationships, managing to the best solution, and user friendly always. Qualifications Required Qualifications And Experience Terminal Degree (where applicable) or degrees including areas of expertise: Certification(s) as applicable. Experience in university level instruction. Experience in other areas,( e.g., clinical, curriculum development, management) Experience teaching in on-line environment, where applicable. Preferred Qualifications 5 years’ experience in university level instruction. Experience with curriculum assessment and program review. Experience in multiple modalities of curriculum development and delivery. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
