    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/80565": {
      "title": "Assistant Head Coach, Women's Wrestling",
      "description": "Assistant Head Coach, Women's Wrestling (4334) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Head Coach, Women's Wrestling (4334) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Apply Description Purpose The Assistant Coach – Women’s Wrestling is responsible for having an in-depth understanding of all aspects that relate to the Women’s Wrestling program, as well as the ongoing recruitment of and development of student-athletes at Life University.  The Assistant Coach performs responsibilities in alignment with the department vision of being a leading institution in performance and meaningful student-athlete experience, and consistently demonstrates valued behaviors of respect, grit, constant growth, and integrity. This position will oversee the Women’s Wrestling program in the absence of the Head Coach. Essential Position Functions Have clear understanding of the values, strategy, and operational plan for the wrestling team under the leadership of the Head Coach. Assist in the coaching/supervision of daily practices and on-mat development including off-season development. This includes meeting performance expectations for team. Assist with recruitment activities for student athletes as directed by the head coach Assist with the organization of team travel as directed by the head coach Work with department administrators in respective areas to ensure the wrestling student-athletes are meeting their athletic and academic responsibilities Assist in all efforts to promote the academic success and engagement of student-athletes including making progress toward their degree As directed by the head coach, participate in meetings with the coaching staff, athletic trainers, and university staff to ensure coherent communication throughout the organization Other duties as assigned by the Head Coach/Athletic Director Fulfill campus liaison duties, if applicable, for entire Department of Athletics as assigned by the Director of Athletics The Assistant Coach is also expected to work with the Head Coach in the successful execution of the deliverables for the Women’s Wrestling program: Execution of business deliverables: Successful planning and monitoring of program budget Plan and execute fundraising initiatives Oversee scholarship distribution to student athletes within allotted parameters Maintain required roster size Execution of performance deliverables: Sustain a competitive program that competes within the conference landscape and competing for bid(s) to the national tournament. Ensure a high level of academic engagement and performance in the classroom, resulting in a team GPA as set by the Director of Athletics, and the graduation of student-athletes. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Exhibit Life University standards of lasting purpose Attitude of helpfulness and gratitude Manage to the best solution Personally commit to building relationships User friendly always Exhibit student-centeredness in performance of all job duties Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Education, Training and/or Experience Bachelor’s degree. Previous collegiate coaching and recruiting experience. Ability to demonstrate overall business acumen. Basic knowledge of the National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) rules and regulations. Ability to interact effectively in a collegial environment. Certifications, Licenses, Registrations CPR/AED certified PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Two (2) years of experience in coaching and recruiting experience Working knowledge and understanding of NAIA/NCAA rules and policies Proficient with statistical/scoring software programs PHYSICAL DEMANDS Ability to lift/carry/relocate equipment and supplies to various locations for athletic events Ability to drive to various locations Ability to demonstrate skills/techniques to student-athletes WORKING CONDITIONS Work performed in various locations in and around the Life University campus, including athletic fields and gymnasiums Travel required Weekend & evening work is required. Must be flexible to accommodate a fast-paced and time demanding profession Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/39C3B08FA765F09BC547D09C6AC939C8/jobs/80573": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant I - COC (4335) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Administrative Assistant I - COC (4335) Main Campus - Marietta, GA 30060 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level High School Category Admin - Clerical Apply Description JOB PURPOSE The Administrative Assistant provides comprehensive administrative and operational support to the College of Chiropractic. This position supports the Dean’s Office, faculty, administrators, students, and visitors by coordinating schedules, preparing correspondence and documents, maintaining records, responding to inquiries, and supporting the school’s daily academic and administrative activities. The Administrative Assistant serves as a primary point of contact for the school and is expected to provide courteous, responsive, and professional customer service. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, discretion, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced academic environment. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS Administrative Support Provide general administrative support to the Dean, school administrators, faculty, and other designated personnel. Manage calendars, schedule appointments, coordinate meetings, and assist with meeting preparation. Prepare agendas, reports, presentations, correspondence, spreadsheets, and other documents. Record and distribute meeting minutes when requested. Draft, proofread, format, and distribute routine communications. Receive, sort, and distribute departmental mail and electronic correspondence. Maintain organized electronic and paper files in accordance with University recordkeeping requirements. Order and maintain office supplies and assist with monitoring departmental inventory. Submit and track routine administrative requests, forms, invoices, purchase requests, and reimbursements. Assist with special projects and other administrative assignments as needed. Scheduling and Academic Support Assist with preparing and maintaining academic, faculty, meeting, and departmental schedules. Coordinate room reservations and schedule changes with the appropriate University departments. Communicate approved schedule information and changes to faculty, administrators, students, and other stakeholders. Assist faculty and administrators with preparing materials for meetings, classes, orientations, accreditation activities, and school events. Support the collection, organization, and maintenance of course, faculty, and departmental information. Track deadlines and provide reminders regarding required documents, meetings, reports, and school activities. Assist with faculty onboarding, orientation, and access to appropriate school and University resources. Help coordinate faculty meetings, professional development activities, student events, and other College of Chiropractic programs. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Customer Service and Communication Serve as a welcoming and professional first point of contact for the College of Chiropractic. Respond to telephone calls, emails, visitors, and routine requests in a timely and courteous manner. Provide general information regarding school operations, schedules, procedures, and available resources. Direct students, faculty, employees, and visitors to the appropriate individual, office, or University resource. Exercise sound judgment when responding to questions and appropriately escalate sensitive, urgent, or complex matters. Build effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and other University departments. Maintain professionalism and composure when addressing competing priorities or difficult customer-service situations. Records and Information Management Maintain accurate faculty, departmental, scheduling, meeting, and operational records. Enter, update, and retrieve information from University systems and databases. Assist with compiling information and preparing routine reports. Monitor the completeness and accuracy of documents before submission or distribution. Handle confidential and sensitive information with appropriate discretion. Follow applicable University policies and requirements concerning student, faculty, employee, and institutional information. Operational Support Assist with coordinating school meetings, events, orientations, and other activities. Reserve meeting spaces and coordinate basic logistical needs, including technology, materials, attendance lists, and refreshments when applicable. Support departmental purchasing and expense-processing activities. Work collaboratively with Academic Affairs, Registrar, Human Resources, Information Technology, Facilities, Events, and other University departments. Identify routine administrative issues and recommend practical solutions or process improvements. Perform other duties consistent with the purpose and responsibilities of the position. PERFORMANCE EXPECTATIONS Successful performance in this position includes: Accurate and timely completion of administrative assignments. Reliable management of schedules, documents, records, and deadlines. Professional and responsive service to faculty, students, administrators, and visitors. Effective communication and collaboration across University departments. Appropriate handling of confidential or sensitive information. Consistent follow-through, dependability, and attention to detail. Positive support of the College of Chiropractic and Life University’s mission. Qualifications KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES Strong organizational and time-management skills. Advanced attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Proficiency in preparing professional correspondence, reports, spreadsheets, presentations, and meeting materials. Ability to learn and use University systems, policies, and procedures. Ability to organize schedules involving multiple individuals, locations, and competing priorities. Ability to anticipate administrative needs and follow through on assignments. Ability to communicate effectively with individuals from different roles, departments, and backgrounds. Ability to remain professional, flexible, and solutions-oriented during periods of change or high activity. Ability to identify matters requiring immediate attention and appropriately involve the responsible administrator. Commitment to supporting the mission, values, and educational environment of Life University. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS High school diploma or equivalent. At least three years of administrative support, office coordination, customer service, or related experience. Strong proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Experience managing calendars, scheduling meetings, preparing documents, and maintaining records. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to provide professional and responsive customer service. Ability to manage multiple assignments, establish priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain attention to detail. Ability to handle sensitive and confidential information appropriately. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a team environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Associate degree or higher. Administrative experience in higher education, healthcare education, an academic department, or a professional school. Experience supporting faculty, academic leaders, or senior administrators. Experience with academic scheduling, student information systems, document-management systems, or enterprise administrative systems. Experience coordinating meetings, orientations, or departmental events. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
